# Prettier defaults its --ignore-path to .gitignore AND .prettierignore, and this repo's .gitignore
# does not list .claude/ — so without this file the repo script walks it.
#
# WHY THAT MATTERS ONLY SINCE ITEM 96. The CI gate used to be `prettier --check "src/**/*.java"`,
# anchored at src/ and therefore immune. Item 96 pointed it at `npm run prettier:check`, whose glob
# `{,**/}*.{md,json,yml,html,java}` leads with `**/` and reaches any depth — including
# `.claude/worktrees/agent-*/`, where an agent keeps a SECOND COMPLETE COPY of this repository while
# it is mid-cycle. Measured 2026-09-13 in this repo by the agent that made the widening, before it landed: a misformatted `.claude/probe/zz.md` is reported by the repo
# script and ignored by the old narrow invocation.
#
# CI is unaffected either way — a clean checkout has no `.claude/` — so the cost is local: a
# developer or agent running the script in the primary checkout while a worktree exists gets warnings
# about files that are not theirs, or reformats a copy nobody will commit.
#
# This is the ESLint `.claude/` finding (backlog item 90) one tool along, and the general rule the
# workspace guide states: a tool that walks the repository from its root now has a second application
# inside it whenever an agent is mid-cycle.
.claude/
